{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a","id":1421703,"title":"Scion Q & A","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-03T17:43:50-08:00","id":1421703,"title":"Scion Q & A","content":"So I've been coming up with a number of questions regarding Scion 2e &amp; I've decided to start a thread focusing on them. If anyone has any questions they want to ask, you can absolutely post them on this thread if you want to. The below link is attached links to what I believe is the first Scion 2e question I asked, &amp; the link after that is for the second. Later posts will feature the questions that I've thought of since.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417506-denizen-scions-a-question\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417506-denizen-scions-a-question\"> Denizen Scions: A Question - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417506-denizen-scions-a-question\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417506-denizen-scions-a-question </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Suppose a Denizen becomes a Scion. Suppose this Denizen's Supernatural Origin Path is exclusive to a single culture. Is the Denizen capable of becoming Scion to any </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421493-titans-scions-virtues\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421493-titans-scions-virtues\"> Titans, Scions &amp; Virtues - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421493-titans-scions-virtues\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421493-titans-scions-virtues </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Going through Titanomachy &amp;amp; I've just realized that I can't tell whether Titanic Scions have virtues or not. I'm getting the implication that their supposed to </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T20:22:26-08:00","id":1421728,"title":"","content":"So, looking through the questions I've got so far, one springs out as being ready to be asked.<br /> <br /> Are the Lovecraft Pantheon going to be having anything in the way of Titans, &amp; might they be considered different from the deities of the Lovecraft Pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T21:49:10-08:00","id":1421735,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, I don't know as much about either Masks of the Mythos beyond it existing (mostly due to lack of interest) and I know even less about Lovecraft (again, due to lack of interest) but if you twisted my arm to guess (again, guess, as I don't know what the book will assume and this is all assumptions) I'd assume that like... In the Masks of the Mythos book, there won't be much in the way of a God/Titan Divide because most of the Lovecraft Entities range from dispassionate indifference towards humanity to outright malice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T21:58:40-08:00","id":1421736,"title":"","content":"Can Titanic Scions take Titanic Callings that are not provided by their patron Titan?<br /> <br /> Is it possible for regular Scions to get Titanic Callings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T22:01:22-08:00","id":1421737,"title":"","content":"The rules for a Scion are that you need to inherit one (1) Calling from your Patron. So if you wanted to play a Scion of Utgard-Loki who has the Destroyer Calling, go for it.<br /> <br /> And as you build your Legend, you can have the Callings that fit your character. Honestly I ignore the moments of &quot;Some Pantheons may find taking these Callings a bit ominous&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T22:55:55-08:00","id":1426290,"title":"","content":"Can Titanic Scions learn Signature Purviews? (With the assumption that they would still be limited by what pantheon their tied to). <br /> <br /> There are some dragons among the gods &amp; Titans, that became gods or Titans. Is it possible (or going to be possible) for a dragon to make that jump in more recent times?<br /> <br /> When Titan Scions elevate to full divine status (past the demigod level), do they become Titans, titanspawn, of gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T01:29:02-08:00","id":1426297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1421728#post1421728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, looking through the questions I've got so far, one springs out as being ready to be asked.<br /> <br /> Are the Lovecraft Pantheon going to be having anything in the way of Titans, &amp; might they be considered different from the deities of the Lovecraft Pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm...I dunno, the Elders as gods for a Scion game? Well...maybe? TBH they're not exactly what I would consider the material for a myth building Scion campaign as chosen/offspring/etc of the gods within a Heroic or Bronze genre. IMHO the Lovecraftian mythos has all the mythic dials set to Iron save Titanomachy, which I'd put at Silver or perhaps Gold if I really wanted to make my players nervous. While one <i>could</i> readily assign them the status of Titans, I tend to think of them more as Primordials, primarily because they're so very alien and outside of the frame of reference puny mortals can fit divinity into. <br /> <br /> That said, them having Scions I'd say are Chosen, as those Elder Gods weren't all that up on the concept of procreation, that was something usually their spawn/minions would muck about with, or cultist subjecting some poor victim to be the receptacle of some metaphysical seed of.. But TBH, I don't see them as the sort of mythos that a Scion campaign would benefit a lot from having present.. Lovecraftian mythos is all about mortals encountering these ancient alien entities and steadily going insane as a result of realizing the shits real, or trying to figure out how to rid the world of crazed cultists intent on hastening the end of the world for whatever imagined benefit. But that's probably a narrow viewpoint based on playing/running Cthulhu games that are faithful to the books.<br /> <br /> So in the spirit of being helpful instead of a naysayer, if I <i>did</i> use the Lovecraftian mythos, I'd rank them as top tier Titans who are so far out there and alien that the rest of a game world's pantheons regard as a universal enemy even more threatening their own Titans. The Devas might not give a damn if Aniwye is stinking up the Cali coastline, they'd rather keep an eye on Rangda, but the moment minions of Nyarlathotep or old Yoggy start to show, they dispatch any and all they can to buddy up with any other Scions and investigate with extreme prejudice.<br /> <br /> Scion's of Lovecraftian gods should also (IMHO at least) be a little out there, you know? Like...they got a knack that lets them have a 12 foot tentacle tongue complete with sucker pods and the ability to ambulate through ala city Spiderman style, and oh yeah, knock the bejesus out of you. Or they they can speak in &quot;tongues&quot; revealing mind breaking truths that causes a listener's sanity to crumble like a cheap, dried out cookie. A Scion's sanity would be more resilient than say a Mortals, but I'd still make a risk so that players would harbor a certain dread, Complications serve this idea pretty well with Resolution being keeping the damn things on <i>their</i> side of the fence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1421737#post1421737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for a Scion are that you need to inherit one (1) Calling from your Patron. So if you wanted to play a Scion of Utgard-Loki who has the Destroyer Calling, go for it.<br /> <br /> And as you build your Legend, you can have the Callings that fit your character. Honestly I ignore the moments of &quot;Some Pantheons may find taking these Callings a bit ominous&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Kyman201 here, i too ignore the notion that Pantheons cock a eyebrow and stroke their chin at a Scion Titan having a calling from their parent. Sure, if all 3 were the same as their parent, that's where they start to whisper in each other's ear, but from what I've made sense of so far (assuming the pantheon in question doesn't outright chant &quot;DIE DIE DIE&quot; at the mere whiff of them) is that while a Scion is the seed/chosen of a given Titan, they can just as readily be a worthy addition to the Pantheon as not, since Scions are divinity in the making and capable of making their own choices as to what they decide to represent or being champions of. In my games at least, they'd judge such a Scion by their deeds and regard them as ally/enemy accordingly.<br /> <br /> Hell, a Titan Scion who hates their progenitor and will always take up arms against their own creator would make for a great redemption theme.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T03:38:11-08:00","id":1426307,"title":"","content":"Hi together,<br /> <br /> here is a little question that came up in recnt Scion game:<br /> <br /> Can Buildings be Birhtrights?<br /> <br /> Background:<br /> <br /> On of my players is huge Dark Anthology fan and wanted for his Scion of Osiris a House like the curator has in the games. His idea was that parts of the foundation were made from fragments of an Temple of Osiris thus giving the Mansion the Death Purview with the Motif &quot;The words of the Master beckon the dead&quot;.<br /> <br /> Most of us at the table see no problem with the idea in itself but disagree on how many points a Birthright like this is worth.<br /> <br /> Thanks in Advance<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T03:47:49-08:00","id":1426309,"title":"","content":"If you guys don\u2019t see any problem it\u2019s ok.<br /> <br /> I personally would treat it as a Guide, and work the cost as one, basically it\u2019s a Purview, so 2 dots.<br /> <br /> Unless you can only use the purview inside the building... then it\u2019s a bit more useless if the adventures never happen out of the building, or as powerful as a guide if the adventures are always inside the building. If it\u2019s a mix of both give half the regular cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T10:09:26-08:00","id":1426333,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T14:44:35-08:00","id":1426860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1421737#post1421737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as you build your Legend, you can have the Callings that fit your character. Honestly I ignore the moments of &quot;Some Pantheons may find taking these Callings a bit ominous&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to get my two cents on that bit. Honestly I viewed it less as &quot;Wait they just took Titan callings, that could be a bad sign because it means they're looking at becoming a Titan.&quot; and interpreted it more as &quot;Might be a bit paranoid, but is anyone else worried that Athena's kid there just declared themself a Destroyer? I'm a bit worried about what might be getting planned since they seem to really have taken to the war aspect of Athena's portfolio.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T04:07:33-08:00","id":1427444,"title":"","content":"Hey guys i got a question.<br /> <br /> Can attributes and skills be raised above five points via experience points?<br /> <br /> A player asked me that yestarday and i didnt know how answer it, since in WOD games the power attribute( blood potency,primal urge), controls that. In Scion its legend ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T11:33:18-08:00","id":1427472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1427444#post1427444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys i got a question.<br /> <br /> Can attributes and skills be raised above five points via experience points?<br /> <br /> A player asked me that yestarday and i didnt know how answer it, since in WOD games the power attribute( blood potency,primal urge), controls that. In Scion its legend ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, getting 5 dots is the maximum you can have in either Attribute or Skill. In order to increase your capacity further than that you use Purviews, Specialties, Knacks and Feats of Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 12-06-2020, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T09:07:55-08:00","id":1427601,"title":"","content":"If i play a solo game, should i increase the number of active knacks that a scion can have active at the same time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T19:15:22-08:00","id":1429584,"title":"","content":"The Shen in 1e had this &quot;caseworker&quot; option for making Scions. Will this option be making a comeback at some point in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T21:54:10-08:00","id":1429714,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'm feeling festive af right now and I wanted to make Santa Claus (As a mantle of Odin) Didn't feel it was right to make an entire new thread for a single homebrew thing but I didn't know where else to post this.<br /> <br /> Santa Claus (Mantle of Odin)<br /> Callings: Creator, Guardian, Liminal<br /> Purviews: Passion (Joy), Frost, Journeys, Artistry, Forge<br /> <br /> Good, Bad, Fugly, how is it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26581-elbrothermouse","name":"ElBrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26581_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T22:19:12-08:00","id":1429715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElBrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1429714#post1429714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I'm feeling festive af right now and I wanted to make Santa Claus (As a mantle of Odin) Didn't feel it was right to make an entire new thread for a single homebrew thing but I didn't know where else to post this.<br /> <br /> Santa Claus (Mantle of Odin)<br /> Callings: Creator, Guardian, Liminal<br /> Purviews: Passion (Joy), Frost, Journeys, Artistry, Forge<br /> <br /> Good, Bad, Fugly, how is it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What's the connection to Odin? My Santa Claus lore is quite murky but isn't Santa Claus originally a Christian Saint from Anatolia or something that got transmuted into Santa Claus of today by Coca Cola?<br /> <br /> The Callings and Purviews are perfect though. Maybe he should have some sort of ability to see if people have been good or bad as well?<br /> <br /> If you stat out Santa then you should probably have Krampus there as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T01:34:36-08:00","id":1429724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElBrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1429714#post1429714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I'm feeling festive af right now and I wanted to make Santa Claus (As a mantle of Odin)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/335850/Noel-Pantheon\" target=\"_blank\">community content about Christmas Pantheon</a>, on real world Christmas figures Santa Claus, P\u00e8re No\u00ebl, Krampus, the Yule Lads, or Frau Holle ( and few more ). It's even Pay What You Want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T02:31:09-08:00","id":1429727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1429715#post1429715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What's the connection to Odin? My Santa Claus lore is quite murky but isn't Santa Claus originally a Christian Saint from Anatolia or something that got transmuted into Santa Claus of today by Coca Cola?<br /> <br /> The Callings and Purviews are perfect though. Maybe he should have some sort of ability to see if people have been good or bad as well?<br /> <br /> If you stat out Santa then you should probably have Krampus there as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long story short, the many folk characters that influenced Santa Claus are all based on Odin in some manner. Hell the eight reindeer of Santa's sleigh are an evolution of Odin's eight hooved steed Sleipnir. I was writing a Scion fan fiction and I was doing a christmas special bit with Odin as Santa. Wanted to whip up some homebrew for the threads I post it in. Badass Santa is always awesome IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1429724#post1429724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/335850/Noel-Pantheon\" target=\"_blank\">community content about Christmas Pantheon</a>, on real world Christmas figures Santa Claus, P\u00e8re No\u00ebl, Krampus, the Yule Lads, or Frau Holle ( and few more ). It's even Pay What You Want.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually good to know, may just pick it up after christmas. NGL I am very tempted to run a Christmas in July adventure for my own scion game. Well, if my group even gets to that. Hell I could probably fit it in as the next adventure of my Scion: Atlantis (as in the disney movie) pulp themed chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26581-elbrothermouse","name":"ElBrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26581_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T02:37:14-08:00","id":1429728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1429715#post1429715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What's the connection to Odin? My Santa Claus lore is quite murky but isn't Santa Claus originally a Christian Saint from Anatolia or something that got transmuted into Santa Claus of today by Coca Cola?<br /> <br /> The Callings and Purviews are perfect though. Maybe he should have some sort of ability to see if people have been good or bad as well?<br /> <br /> If you stat out Santa then you should probably have Krampus there as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a more in-depth rundown of the connections between Odin and Santa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://sonsofvikings.com/blogs/history/viking-origins-of-christmas-yule-traditions\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://sonsofvikings.com/cdn/shop/articles/santa-odin-comparison_cdefe0bd-198f-4174-83b1-ca6469d19a42_1024x1024.jpg?v=1764260386\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sonsofvikings.com/blogs/history/viking-origins-of-christmas-yule-traditions\" target=\"_blank\"> Santa and Odin - Christmas and Yule </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sonsofvikings.com/blogs/history/viking-origins-of-christmas-yule-traditions\" target=\"_blank\"> https://sonsofvikings.com/blogs/history/viking-origins-of-christmas-yule-traditions </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Thanks for visiting our blog! As a thank-you, enjoy 15% off your first order in our online&nbsp;Viking Shop with the discount code BLOG15. New updates! Revised 11/14/22.&nbsp;Originally posted on 12/15/17. Was&nbsp;Santa Claus partially inspired by&nbsp;Odin?&nbsp; First things first:1) No, we are not saying Odin is Santa, or that Santa is Odi </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oh, and if you really want some Scion flavor, here's Santa as a Scion, written by the guy who wrote The Wizard of Oz books<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus-Baum_%281902%29_0001.png/960px-The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus-Baum_%281902%29_0001.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus\" target=\"_blank\"> The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It even got one of those Rankin Bass stop-motion adaptions!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus_(1985_film)\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/The_Life_%26_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus_(1985_film)\" target=\"_blank\"> The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus (1985 film) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus_(1985_film)\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Life_and_Adventures_of_Santa_Claus_(1985_film) </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":25851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","user":"TheStray7","date":". 12-24-2020, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T03:13:37-08:00","id":1429733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElBrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1429727#post1429727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Long story short, the many folk characters that influenced Santa Claus are all based on Odin in some manner. Hell the eight reindeer of Santa's sleigh are an evolution of Odin's eight hooved steed Sleipnir. I was writing a Scion fan fiction and I was doing a christmas special bit with Odin as Santa. Wanted to whip up some homebrew for the threads I post it in. Badass Santa is always awesome IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I did not know that. I've always considered Santa Claus a mashup of Christian and British pagan mythology, especially Father Christmas from England.<br /> <br /> Odin and Santa Claus seem like complete polar opposites as characters. But maybe that's why Odin is such a grumpy and mean person in mythology; he extracted and isolated every little fragment of generousity and kindness into one of his mantles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T06:44:13-08:00","id":1430452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1427601#post1427601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i play a solo game, should i increase the number of active knacks that a scion can have active at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the feel you want for the game. I probably would adjust the antagonists and obstacles down in power a bit rather than adding knacks. That lets me as SG fine-tune things easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:42:54-07:00","id":1439932,"title":"","content":"So I was just reading through Scion: Titanomachy &amp; I noticed something that didn't fit.<br /> F\u016bjin's Callings are listed as &quot;Destroyer, Fortune, Primeval&quot;.<br /> The problem here is that Fortune is a Purview, not a Calling.<br /> So my question is: what would be an appropriate Calling to slot in here? Me, I'm thinking either Guardian or Warrior based on his write up, but I was wondering whether anyone else had any better ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T01:04:38-07:00","id":1439981,"title":"","content":"The correct Callings of Fujin are Destroyer Leader Primeval.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a nother note does anyone know if Relics that grant purviews also grant the associated innate powers?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T01:16:46-07:00","id":1439982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mugbearer23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421703-scion-q-a?p=1439981#post1439981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a nother note does anyone know if Relics that grant purviews also grant the associated innate powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. If you have access to the purview you always get the associated innate power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T02:17:34-07:00","id":1439987,"title":"","content":"Does this also go for Mythos Scions? I mean based on the preview Manuscripts it seems like they can only ever acquire one Innate power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T04:31:30-07:00","id":1440003,"title":"","content":"If they get one they don\u2019t get the other, they are the exception, but yet they get one innate power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T04:44:42-07:00","id":1440005,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> Seems a bit unbalanced since the Awareness Innate powers are not that OP so i wasnt quite sure if i understood it correctly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}